---
description: Game feel principles — the player must always feel something happening
globs:
  - "client/src/**"
---

- Target feel: Brawl Stars / Clash Royale polish, Coin Master casino
  excitement, chaotic party energy. If a moment feels flat, add anticipation
  (wind-up), impact (shake/flash/sound) and follow-through (settle bounce).
- Money must feel physical: coins arc, spin, land, stack and burst. Score
  changes always animate (ticker roll + floating text), never teleport.
- The camera is a storyteller: drift when idle, punch on lock-in, zoom for
  reveals, shake on impacts, pull back for standings. Keep it subtle in
  `reduced` mode.
- Escalate drama with stakes: bigger losses -> angrier reactions and stronger
  effects; big wins -> coin bursts and celebration.
- Sound events accompany every meaningful action through `SoundEventBus`
  (synth blips now, samples later — same event names).
- Preserve type safety and 60fps: pool or self-destroy effect objects, avoid
  per-frame allocations in `update()`.
